      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I noticed that there are a few places where the length is capped at `MAX_RW_COUNT` which is defined as `INT_MAX \u0026 PAGE_MASK`.\n\nI believe the `rw_verify_area()` check would catch anything larger, since the check where it casts the count to a `ssize_t` will result in a negative value if `count` is larger than `MAX_RW_COUNT`, but instead of catching it that late, should we catch that here? That would mean limiting this function to a max of ~2 GB.\n\nWould that be a problem? Do we expect buffers to be that big?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "59db38a85287139bd8b24fe30381260b9ce80df9",
